Fixes wishlist add-to-wishlist requests silently being processed with stale
data for every product except the very first one added after a customer
logs in.

Root cause: when a guest tries to add a product to the wishlist,
Magento\Wishlist\Controller\Index\Plugin::beforeDispatch() blocks the
request and stores its params in the customer session under both
before_wishlist_request and before_request_params (the latter so
Wishlist\Controller\Index\Add::execute() can replay the original request
after login, per the already-applied fix-adding-to-wishlist.patch). After
the customer logs in, the same beforeDispatch() restores the request from
before_wishlist_request and clears it with unsBeforeWishlistRequest() -
but before_request_params is never cleared anywhere in the codebase.

Because Add::execute() prefers before_request_params over the current
request params whenever it is non-empty, this stale value keeps being used
for every subsequent add-to-wishlist AJAX call for the rest of the customer
session, regardless of which product was actually clicked. The affected
requests return HTTP 200 with no JS errors, which makes the failure look
like a silent server-side/session issue rather than an obvious bug.

Fix: clear before_request_params together with before_wishlist_request
once it has been consumed.

diff --git a/Controller/Index/Plugin.php b/Controller/Index/Plugin.php
index 81d9276..3a4eb10 100644
--- a/Controller/Index/Plugin.php
+++ b/Controller/Index/Plugin.php
@@ -133,6 +133,7 @@ class Plugin
                 $request->clearParams();
                 $request->setParams($data);
                 $this->customerSession->unsBeforeWishlistRequest();
+                $this->customerSession->unsBeforeRequestParams();
             } elseif ($request->getParam('token')) {
                 // check if the token is valid and retrieve the data
                 $data = $this->dataSerializer->unserialize($request->getParam('token'));
